# Auth-Service Non-Negotiables

## Institutional Email Only

- Login and password reset flows must accept ONLY institutional emails:
  - Domain must end with `@uce.edu.ec`
- Reject other domains with 400 (validation error).
- Never reveal whether a user exists in forgot-password:
  - Always return 200 with a generic message.

## JWT + Refresh Rotation

- Access token short-lived.
- Refresh token long-lived with rotation:
  - On refresh: revoke old refresh, issue new refresh.
  - Support "token family" / session chain to detect reuse.

## Token Storage

- NEVER store raw refresh tokens or raw password reset tokens.
- Store only hashes (+ salt/pepper if configured).
- Store expiry timestamps and revoked/used timestamps.

## RBAC

- Mandatory roles: TEACHER / STUDENT / ADMIN.
- Implement RolesGuard + @Roles decorator.
- /auth/me requires valid access token.

## Rate Limiting

- Enforce per-IP and per-route limits at least for:
  - POST /auth/login
  - POST /auth/refresh
  - POST /auth/forgot-password
- Use Redis for rate limiting counters.

## CORS

- Must be explicit and environment-based.

## No Hardcoded Users

- No hardcoded accounts.
- Dev seed allowed only if gated by NODE_ENV=development and documented.

## Events (Kafka)

Auth-service must emit events (no sensitive data):

- auth.user.logged_in
- auth.user.login_failed (optional but useful)
- auth.user.password_reset_requested
- auth.user.password_reset_completed
  Include correlation_id and actor_user_id when available.
